    },
    "end_date": "2022-07-18",
    "selection_basis": "200 m square centred on the GHNA instrument coordinates in De Vis et al. (2024) Section 2.1.1, using the same cutout width as Section 2.2.4. Select the earliest accepted Sentinel-2 matchup in Table 1 whose preceding rolling baseline starts after the first listed good Sentinel-2 matchup (June 8): July 13, 2022, in target July 11-18 and baseline June 13-July 11. Fixed before any detector result, without searching for a negative satellite output. Published surface stability and independently selected ground samples support a quiet-reference candidate; they do not certify every AOI cell, SAR stability, or equivalence to urban construction/transport land cover.",
    "references": [
      {
        "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/remote-sensing/articles/10.3389/frsen.2024.1323998/full",
        "supports": "GHNA instrument coordinates, stable gravel-plain surface, 200 m satellite cutout method, deployment from May 2022 and accepted July 13 Sentinel-2 / ground-instrument matchup. GHNA is distinct from the nearby GONA RadCalNet station."
      },
      {
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8039303",
        "supports": "Version 1.0.0 independent ground-reflectance sample files. Five fixed sequences on June 22/28/30, July 10 and July 13 were checksum-verified; all quality-valid common five-degree directions and excluded flags are retained in selection evidence."
      }
    ]
  },
